
Observer Design Pattern:
========================
    ○ The Observer Design Pattern defines a ONE-to-MANY relationships between objects.
    ○ When one object(Subject) changes it's state, all its dependents(Observers) are notified automatically.


Where it is used ?
====================
   ○ Event Handling Systems
   ○ Notification Systems
   ○ UI frameworks
   ○ Messaging and Pub/Sub systems

Advantages:
===========
   ○ Decouples the Subject and Observers.
   ○ Easy to add or remove Observers dynamically.
   ○ Works well for event-driven systems.

Interviewer tips:
================
   ○ "How would you design a notification system" ?
      This pattern is your go-to answer.
   ○ In modern systems, this is implemented via event-driven architecture using Kafka, RabbitMQ or Spring Events.
